### 1. Standard Deduction vs. Itemizing
For the 2024 tax year, the **Standard Deduction for Married Filing Jointly is $29,200**. 
Your listed itemized deductions (the $2,000 charitable donation) fall well below this amount. Unless you have significant other itemized deductions (such as high mortgage interest, large medical expenses, or state/local taxes up to the $10,000 cap), it is highly beneficial for you to take the **Standard Deduction**. 

### 2. What You Can Deduct
Even if you take the standard deduction, you can still claim certain "above-the-line" deductions and business expenses:

*   **Student Loan Interest:** You can deduct up to **$2,500** (the IRS maximum per year) of the $2,700 you paid. This is an adjustment to income, meaning you get this deduction on top of your standard deduction.
